.TH LIBUTF8_ENCODE_MEASURE 3 LIBUTF8
.SH NAME
libutf8_encode_measure - Get the number of bytes required to encode a codepoint

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libutf8.h>

size_t \fBlibutf8_encode_measure\fP(uint_least32_t \fIcodepoint\fP);
.fi
.PP
Link with
.IR -lutf8 .

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR libutf8_encode_measure ()
function returns the number of bytes required to encode
.I codepoint
as UTF-8. It returns zero if the codepoint cannot be
represented in 31 bits.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR libutf8_encode_measure ()
function returns the number of bytes required to encode
.IR codepoint ,
or zero if it is unrepresentable.
This value cannot exceed 6, and does not exceed 4 for
codepoint less or equal to
.BR LIBUTF8_ULTIMATE_CODEPOINT (3).

.SH ERRORS
The
.BR libutf8_encode_measure ()
function cannot fail per se, and never sets
.IR errno ;
.B EDOM
is an appropriate value when the function returns zero.

.SH ATTRIBUTES
For an explanation of the terms used in this section, see
.BR attributes (7).
.PP
.TS
allbox;
lb lb lb lb
l l l l.
Interface	Thread safety	Async-signal safety	Async-cancel safety
T{
.BR libutf8_encode_measure ()
T}	MT-Safe	AS-Safe	AC-Safe
.TE
.sp

